    "content": "Very fun, very short, and very simple. I think this a great idea, and would work really well.\n\nHowever, I think you should correct the grammar in the statement though. Maybe reword it to something like, \"You need to analyze <<the quality of>> [[n]] <<metals>>, where [[t]] is the minimum purity, [[p]], required to <<pass the quality test>>. Output {{keep}} if the metal passes the test, or {{discard}} if it doesn't. At the end, output the indexes of the selected metals, all separated by a space, ranging from 0 to [[n]] - 1.\n\nIn the \"Next n lines\" part of the input, you should add [[p]] right after purity.\n\nIn the output, keep and discard should probably be formatted as {{keep}} and {{discard}}.\n\nAlso, in the constraints, you should add a constraint on the variable n.\n\nLastly, I don't know if this is great for reverse mode just because of the last part of the question. I don't know how easy this is to figure out within 5-10 minutes, but I'll leave this up to you.",
    "codingamerHandle": "5ec2966d82c6e219d9431b570a1556910553834",
    "elapsedTime": 53998000
  },
